---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import { ENTITY, CONTACT } from '../lib/legal.js'

/* Everything on this page is checked against the shipping code, not against
   the old site. The claims that are NOT here are as deliberate as the ones
   that are: no "never leaves the machine" (that described v1 — see
   MAC_HANDOFF.md), no promise about how long the speech-to-text provider
   keeps uploaded audio, and no statement about international transfer
   mechanisms. Those belong in the longer policy in prism-aai/docs/legal once
   a lawyer and a legal entity exist. */
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy — Prism"
  description="What Prism does with your recordings, your transcripts and your email address. Plain answers, checked against the shipping app."
  heading="Privacy"
>
  <p>
    Prism listens to your calls. That earns you straight answers about where
    everything goes. This page covers what {ENTITY} collects, what we do with it,
    and how to get rid of it.
  </p>

  <h2>If all you did was ask for access</h2>
  <p>
    The form on this site sends one thing: the email address you typed, plus a
    note of which form it came from. We use it to send you an invite when one is
    available. We do not sell it, rent it, or add you to a marketing list.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no analytics on this website. No Google Analytics, no pixel, no
    advertising tracker, no session recorder. Our host records ordinary web
    server logs, which include IP addresses, and we do not read them for
    anything but keeping the site up.
  </p>
  <p>
    To be taken off the list, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> from
    the address you signed up with and we will delete the row.
  </p>

  <h2>If you use the app</h2>

  <h3>Audio</h3>
  <p>
    Recording starts when you start it. Prism captures your microphone and what
    your computer is playing, as two separate tracks, into files on your own
    machine.
  </p>
  <p>
    When the recording ends, that audio is sent through our relay to a
    speech-to-text provider. <strong>The relay stores no audio.</strong> It passes the
    bytes straight through: nothing is written to disk, nothing is written to
    storage, and nothing about the audio outlives the request. We ask the
    provider to delete the transcript as soon as we have retrieved it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The original recording stays on your computer, inside the note, until you
    delete it.
  </p>

  <h3>Transcripts and notes</h3>
  <p>
    Your transcripts, notes, tasks and folders are stored in your account so
    that your devices stay in step. That is the only reason the account exists.
    Delete a note and it is removed from your account and stops syncing.
  </p>

  <h3>Your account</h3>
  <p>
    Your account holds your email address and the settings you have chosen. You
    sign in with a password, or with a code we email you if you would rather not
    have one.
  </p>

  <h3>The AI providers</h3>
  <p>
    Transcription is done by a speech-to-text provider, and notes are written by
    a large language model provider. They receive the audio or the transcript
    for as long as it takes to do the work. We use paid API tiers, whose terms
    exclude using your content to train models.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We never train on your content, and we never sell it.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Other people on the call</h2>
  <p>
    Prism does not announce itself to anyone else on the call, because nothing
    of ours is in the call. Telling the other people that you are recording is
    your responsibility, and the law on that differs by where you and they are.
    Some places require everyone to agree. Check before you press record.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you were recorded by someone using Prism and want to know what is held
    about you, the person who made the recording controls it, not us. Write to
    them. If you cannot, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> and we will help you reach them.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting things</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A note: delete it in the app. It stops syncing to your other devices.</li>
    <li>The local recording: it sits with the note on your computer and goes when the note does.</li>
    <li>Your account, or your waitlist row: email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Prism is early and this page will get longer as the product does. If
    something material changes about where your recordings go, we will say so
    here and date it, not quietly edit it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
